# Dendry source files must use LF line endings.
#
# The dendrynexus content parser mis-parses CRLF files: its blank-line feature
# regex (^[ \t]*\n) also matches the \n half of a CRLF pair, because in
# multiline mode ^ asserts after \r as well. That turns every line break inside
# a multi-line conditional ([? if cond : ... ?]) into a paragraph break, which
# shatters the conditional and aborts the build with:
#   TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'type')
#     at _extractPredicate (.../parsers/content.js)
#
# Without this rule, Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true get CRLF files
# and `dendrynexus make-html` fails locally even though the committed blobs
# (and CI, which checks out on Linux) are fine.
*.dry text eol=lf
